WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.502 line:0%
And finally, New Rule.
In the future,

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:03.569 line:0%
all American schoolkids

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.871 line:0%
must be made
to study the constitution.

00:00:06.538 --> 00:00:09.775 line:0%
-Not ours, Brazil's.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:00:09.875 --> 00:00:11.444 line:0%
Because plainly,
that one is working

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.112 line:0%
a lot better
than the one we have.

00:00:13.512 --> 00:00:16.483 line:0%
America ran a very clear
scientific experiment

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:17.684 line:0%
with Brazil recently,

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.752 line:0%
where we faced
the exact same situation,

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:22.188 line:0%
and let's just say,
when it comes to democracy,

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:23.956 line:0%
we're the ones who got waxed.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:26.959 line:0%
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-Brazil, you know.

00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:29.262
Yeah. Bolsonaro.
The coup, yeah. Yeah.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:30.530
(BILL MAHER LAUGHS)

00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:33.900
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:36.636
Needed to stroke the audience
more on that one, I guess.

00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:39.405
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-So... (LAUGHS)

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:40.506
So, here's what happened.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.909
In 2020,
American incumbent president,

00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:45.845
Donald Trump, a thrice-married
far-right populist,

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.613
lost his re-election bid.

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:50.116
And then embarked
on a campaign of outright lies

00:00:50.182 --> 00:00:52.652
to convince his supporters
the election had been rigged,

00:00:52.785 --> 00:00:55.354
which resulted in the siege
of the American Capitol

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:56.755
on January 6th.

00:00:56.989 --> 00:01:00.293
(CROWD CHANTING)

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:05.498
Fast forward almost two years
to the day, January 8th, 2023,

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:09.468
and Jair Bolsonaro,
Brazil's thrice-married,

00:01:09.568 --> 00:01:11.737
far-right populist
incumbent president,

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:14.440
known as the Trump
of the tropics, repeats the--

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.675
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-He was.

00:01:16.742 --> 00:01:20.012
Repeats the Trump playbook
exactly after he loses

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:21.380
his re-election bid,

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:23.850
and thousands
of his supporters storm

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:26.685
-the Brazilian capital.
-(INDISTINCT CLAMORING ON VIDEO)

00:01:26.785 --> 00:01:28.120
Both insurrections fail.

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:29.555
But here's
where we see the difference

00:01:29.621 --> 00:01:31.390
between a healthy democracy

00:01:31.523 --> 00:01:33.459
and one that's hanging
by a thread.

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:36.395
After January 8th,
almost all of Brazil

00:01:36.495 --> 00:01:39.765
turned on the plotters
and made Bolsonaro a pariah.

00:01:40.265 --> 00:01:41.467
But after January 6th,

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:44.070
Trump went on
to his winter palace in Florida

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:47.974
to accept tributes
and re-plot in opulent splendor.

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:49.842
-Bolsonaro...
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:51.710
Bolsonaro also went to Florida

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:53.913
where he ate by himself
at a KFC.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.416
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)
-That's a real picture.

00:01:57.516 --> 00:02:01.321
I love you.
I love you, man. (LAUGHS)

00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:05.091
Today, only six percent
of Brazilians

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.660
say they support the mob
that sacked their capital.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:10.329
But in America,
Trump's more popular than ever

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:12.131
and on track to regain power.

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:15.000
In Brazil, not only
has Bolsonaro been banned

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:16.769
from running again
anytime soon,

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:19.072
but the country united
around their new leader,

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:22.141
who walked arm-in-arm
with congressional leaders

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:24.344
from the Left and Right
in solidarity

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.644
against the uprising.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:26.813
Arm-in-arm.

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:29.549
In America, no arm-in-arm.

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:32.852
-Arms, yes.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:35.488
-Plenty of that.
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:36.622
And threats.

00:02:36.722 --> 00:02:39.258
Most Republicans
were literally scared to death

00:02:39.324 --> 00:02:40.426
to do the right thing.

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:42.461
They didn't wanna be hung
like Mike Pence,

00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:44.464
or castrated
like Lindsey Graham.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:49.168
-(SETH MACFARLANE LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.003
Because... (LAUGHS)

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:54.574
The thing is, in Brazil,
their conservative party

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.642
is where ours was
during Watergate,

00:02:57.176 --> 00:02:59.846
when Republicans were willing
to throw Nixon under the bus

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:03.183
because they still had ideals
higher than owning the libs.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:07.152
So, what changed?
Well, part of it's structural.

00:03:07.252 --> 00:03:09.689
Their constitution
is only 35 years old.

00:03:09.755 --> 00:03:15.027
-Ours is 235, and it looks it.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:03:15.127 --> 00:03:17.530
We not only
still use old-timey words

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:19.999
like gerrymandering,
we still practice it.

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:21.901
The average
Republican congressman

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:22.935
is in a safe seat

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.937
with an electorate
he chose himself.

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.173
And he's only scared
of two things.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.241
A primary opponent
with more guns

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:33.645
-on his Christmas card...
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:03:33.712 --> 00:03:35.615
...and getting a nickname
from Trump.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.216
Trump has proven
that in America,

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:39.285
you can absolutely attempt
a coup.

00:03:39.618 --> 00:03:40.486
And at the very least,

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.254
there's no
immediate repercussions.

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:44.557
The only way we are allowed
to punish a president

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:47.626
is through impeachment,
where the jury is the Senate.

00:03:48.193 --> 00:03:52.231
Except California has 68 times
the population of Wyoming,

00:03:52.297 --> 00:03:54.100
and yet we both get
two senators.

00:03:54.433 --> 00:03:56.469
We both get two jurors.

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:58.704
In Brazil,
elections are overseen

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:02.608
by a special electoral court,
with judges who serve two terms.

00:04:02.808 --> 00:04:03.809
We don't have that.

00:04:04.109 --> 00:04:05.678
We have
a partisan Supreme Court

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:08.080
whose terms expire when they do.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:12.084
-(LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:13.586
-(LAUGHS)
-ADAM SCHIFF: It's true.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.558
And who are mostly picked
by presidents

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:21.060
who lost the popular vote.

00:04:21.226 --> 00:04:22.928
And our elections
are run by the states,

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:25.698
so you got a hodgepodge
of 50 different election systems

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.099
with 50 different rule books.

00:04:27.199 --> 00:04:28.634
And we're the only nation
on earth

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:31.804
that chooses their election
by way of an electoral college,

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:34.173
which is somehow even worse
than regular college.

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:40.847
-(LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:43.516
And if all that
isn't bad enough,

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:46.652
it takes America two months
to count and certify the votes,

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:48.287
which gives the losers
plenty of time

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:49.722
to plot and make mischief.

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:53.225
In Brazil,
popular vote always wins.

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:55.761
Everybody goes to the polls
on the same day,

00:04:56.128 --> 00:04:59.064
and the official commission
declares the winner that night.

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:02.235
And then everyone goes outside
and flashes their tits.

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:08.808
-(SETH LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:13.045
As opposed to here,
because about 40 years ago,

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:14.881
we changed
television news gathering

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:17.516
from a public service
to a division of the company

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:18.817
that has to make a profit.

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:23.422
We let various shit-disturbing,
ratings-hungry news outlets

00:05:23.522 --> 00:05:26.392
call the election
and tease out the suspense

00:05:26.458 --> 00:05:29.395
like it's the Golden Bachelor
giving out the final rose.

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:35.468
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:38.537
It used to be people's opinions
were shaped by the news.

00:05:38.737 --> 00:05:41.240
Now, the news is shaped
by people's opinions.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:42.208
Opinions.

00:05:42.341 --> 00:05:44.243
It's all we hear
in the media all day long

00:05:44.376 --> 00:05:46.678
when we're not hearing it
from our friends on Facebook.

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:48.780
-And by friends, I mean--
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:05:48.847 --> 00:05:54.320
-By friends, I mean Russians.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:05:54.586 --> 00:05:55.922
And there's one more thing.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:59.425
We're just a shittier people
than we used to be.

00:05:59.491 --> 00:06:01.193
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-(ADAM LAUGHS)

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:06.065
-Sorry.
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:08.234
Sorry,
but we ran the experiment,

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:09.368
and we lost.

00:06:09.768 --> 00:06:13.939
In Brazil, the politics
of grievance has its limits.

00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:15.374
Here, it doesn't.

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:19.478
There are 172 election deniers
currently sitting in Congress,

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:22.214
but Republicans
only threw out one guy.

00:06:22.581 --> 00:06:24.349
And ironically,
he was from Brazil.

00:06:24.616 --> 00:06:30.189
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)
-(LAUGHS)

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:34.360
So, yes.
Our conservatives deserve

00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:35.594
the lion's share of the blame.

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:37.463
They're the ones
who are sticking with Trump.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.899
But it's also
not that simple, guys.

00:06:40.599 --> 00:06:42.467
It's also the fact
that since Watergate,

00:06:42.567 --> 00:06:44.569
the parties
have flipped personalities.

00:06:44.736 --> 00:06:47.106
Democrats used to be
the party of the working class,

00:06:47.173 --> 00:06:48.875
and Republicans
were the elitist,

00:06:49.141 --> 00:06:50.643
chardonnay-sipping assholes,

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:54.079
the snobs on the winning side
of the diploma divide.

00:06:54.146 --> 00:06:55.414
But that got switched up.

00:06:55.547 --> 00:06:58.584
And people really hate a snob,
enough, in fact,

00:06:58.651 --> 00:07:01.053
to vote for Trump,
who recently said,

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.956
"It's nice to have a strongman
running your country."

00:07:04.823 --> 00:07:07.059
Well, many Brazilians remember
when it wasn't.

00:07:07.727 --> 00:07:09.462
They lived
under a real dictatorship,

00:07:09.528 --> 00:07:10.863
less than 40 years ago.

00:07:11.096 --> 00:07:13.866
And so, they have an immunity
that we do not.

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:16.335
It would be nice
if we could get that immunity

00:07:16.468 --> 00:07:18.037
without having
to get the disease.

